### =====================================================================
### mcp-client-service: the AI shopping assistant
###
### Through the API gateway (as the website will call it). Guests may chat; with a customer's token the conversation
### belongs to that customer. Answers take a few seconds (the model runs on the CPU).
### Needs: Ollama (start-infra.ps1 -Profiles ai), mcp-server-service, mcp-client-service, the gateway and the
### catalog services. Run the requests in VS Code (REST Client extension) or IntelliJ IDEA.
### =====================================================================

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@service = http://localhost:8114

### 1. A guest asks a question: start a new conversation (no conversationId).
###    -> data.answer, data.conversationId, data.grounded = true, data.toolsUsed = ["searchProducts"]
# @name firstQuestion
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Do you have Amul butter? How much is it?"}

### 2. A follow-up in the same conversation ("it" = Amul butter, from the conversation)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"conversationId": "{{firstQuestion.response.body.data.conversationId}}", "message": "Is it in stock?"}

### 3. The messages of the conversation (oldest first)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/conversations/{{firstQuestion.response.body.data.conversationId}}

### 4. Something the shop does not sell -> it searches first, then "could not find"
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Do you sell the iPhone 15?"}

### 5. Delivery rules, offers, stores
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "When is delivery free, and which coupons can I use?"}

### 6. Not about the shop -> polite refusal, no tool, grounded = false
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Who won the cricket world cup in 2011?"}

### 7. Validation: an empty message -> 400 "Please type a message"
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "   "}

### 8. A conversation id that does not exist (or belongs to someone else) -> 404
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{"conversationId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000", "message": "Hi"}

### 9. Log in as customer1 (seed data) ...
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "customer1@grocery.com", "password": "Password@123"}

### 10. ... and chat as that customer: the conversation belongs to user 4 only
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "Where is the Fresh Mart store?"}

### 11. Delete the first conversation ("New chat" in the widget)
DELETE {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/conversations/{{firstQuestion.response.body.data.conversationId}}

### 12. Directly at the service (without the gateway, no chat rate limit): send the user header yourself
POST {{service}}/api/v1/chat/messages
X-User-Id: 4
Content-Type: application/json

{"message": "What is the minimum order value?"}

### 13. Health (used by Kubernetes)
GET {{service}}/actuator/health

### ---------- Voice (speaches: start-infra.ps1 -Profiles ai; docs/ai-assistant-plan.md "Voice") ----------
### A spoken question takes three calls: the recording -> its words (14), the words -> the answer (1), the answer -> speech (15).
### question.webm (next to this file) says "Which offers are running this week?", recorded the way Chrome and Edge do.

### 14. A recording becomes text -> data.text "Which offers are running this week."
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/transcriptions
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=voice

--voice
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="audio"; filename="question.webm"
Content-Type: audio/webm

< ./question.webm
--voice--

### 15. An answer is read aloud -> audio/mpeg (the "Accept" lets errors still come back as JSON)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/speech
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: audio/mpeg, application/json

{"text": "Fresh Mart has Amul Butter at ₹58.00 for 100 g. Orders above ₹299 are delivered free."}

### 16. Nothing to read aloud -> 400 (JSON, also when audio was asked for)
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/chat/speech
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: audio/mpeg, application/json

{"text": " "}
